/T (By mid-2025, 226,506 people in Germany were under an obligation to leave, of whom 184,988 were tolerated \(~80%\) \(Deutscher Bundestag, 2025a, p. 35\). This represents a decline from 248,145 tolerated individuals at the end of 2022, before the Opportunity Residence Right was introduced, with the reduction attributed both to the programme and to an increase in deportations. )
