398 0 obj
<<
/Title (By mid-2025, 226,506 people in Germany were under an obligation to leave, of whom 184,988 were tolerated \(~80%\) \(Deutscher Bundestag, 2025a, p. 35\). This represents a decline from 248,145 tolerated individuals at the end of 2022, before the Opportunity Residence Right was introduced, with the reduction attributed both to the programme and to an increase in deportations.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 360 0 R
/Next 399 0 R
>>
endobj
399 0 obj
<<
/Title (As of May 2025, 84,106 people had received the Opportunity Residence Right. Of these, 16,646 had successfully transitioned to a long-term residence permit \(~19%\), while 31,372 remained within the 18-month grant period \(~37%\) \(Mediendienst Integration, 2025\).)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 360 0 R
/Prev 398 0 R
>>
